/*  dirHeadT -- insertAt with where=before on the FIRST LINE of a buffer.

    ⚠ BORN RED ON PURPOSE AND GRADUATED THE SAME DAY (H7, then H6). It is
    F-67's residue, and it only became visible on 2026-09-16: until the `*where`
    star landed in incant/directives, where=before never fired at all, so the
    first-line case could not be reached to be wrong. It was pinned to the RIGHT
    answer rather than to the broken one, deliberately, so that the repair would
    turn it green without anyone having to notice. It did, within the hour.

    THE DEFECT IT WAS BORN ON: the payload landed ONE CHARACTER INTO the first
    line -- `hHEAD-PAYLOAD` then `eadLine alpha`.

    THE REPAIR, one line in getMarkLineAt (Instruct.rtn): the walk ended with
    `if lineStart >= start lineStart++;`, and lineStart can never be BELOW start,
    so the ++ always fired. For a line reached by walking back to a \n that step
    is right, because it steps over the newline; for the first line the walk
    stops at start and the step goes into the text. It now asks what the walk
    actually stopped ON -- `if lineStart == '\n' lineStart++;` -- which is right
    in both positions and makes the dead `else lineStart = start;` unnecessary.

    ⚠ IT HAS ITS OWN SAMPLE AND ITS OWN RUN because getFile is once per FIELD
    and the buffer mark only ever ADVANCES -- a head case cannot share a buffer
    with anything, since everything else is forward of it.

    Sentinel at the foot, single stop.  */
Start();
include(directives);

register(Directives);
define
    source="incant/dirHeadSample";
    dHead source fromThis="headLine" toThis='HEAD-PAYLOAD\n' where=before;
    ;

getFile(source);
insertAt(dHead);
print ``"=== head, where=before ===":source:;
print "DIRHEADT SENTINEL":;
stop();
